---
description: Core project behavior for AI-assisted development
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read relevant project documentation before substantial changes.
- Search for existing implementations before creating duplicate components or services.
- Preserve existing functionality unless the task explicitly requires changing it.
- Never hard-code secrets or credentials.
- Treat legacy projects, purchased templates, and Figma as references to adapt.
- Prefer portable infrastructure abstractions; avoid coupling domain logic to AWS, Docker, Plesk, or a specific hosting provider.
- Record significant architecture decisions under docs/decisions.
